1 NOTE Ahnentafel position 16.
1 NOTE 1881 Leopoldina lottery consortium (NWS-0004): "Simplicio José Ferreira Armond" is listed among the members of a "Grande Loteria da Côrte" ticket consortium held by his father-in-law Ladisláo Egídio Ferreira de Toledo (P-0056), alongside several Toledos. Corroborates his presence in the Leopoldina Toledo circle in 1881 — earlier than his 1899/1902 Muriaé police offices — and confirms this is the Toledo son-in-law, not the elder Barbacena namesake.
1 NOTE Parents UNKNOWN. Simplício's Armond surname distinguishes him from the Toledo family he married into. PRB-0008 and PRB-0009 (1867 inventários) list a "Simplício José Ferreira de TOLEDO, solteiro, 14 anos" as JC's own son (item 6 in both) — a DIFFERENT person with a Toledo surname who died before 1879. A prior session (7 August 2026) mistakenly identified that Simplício de Toledo with our Simplício Armond and added F-0026 as his birth family; corrected same day. He is Eliza Balbina de Toledo's husband; his biological parents remain unidentified. He is NOT a child of José Cezário de Toledo Lima (P-0054) or Claudina Brandina de Jesus (P-0055).
1 NOTE His name appears in four records: the short "Simplicio Armand" (Aristão's 1957 death, CIV-0005); "Simplício Ferreira Armond" (Marfiza's 1962 death, CIV-0013); and "Simplicio José Ferreira Armond" (the 1881 Toledo heir list PRB-0001 and the 1884 petition PRB-0002) — PRB-0002 bearing his own autograph signature ("Simplicio Joze Ferr.a Armond"). The owner confirms his full name is "Simplício José Ferreira Armond", set as the preferred name on 2026-07-30 — it matches his autograph signature and the two 1880s probate records; the shorter source forms ("Simplicio Armand", "Simplício Ferreira Armond") are preserved as variants.
1 NOTE Public office (1899, 1902): named 2.º supplente do subdelegado of the Boa Família district, Muriaé, by an act published in the Minas Geraes state gazette of 28 July 1899 (GOV-0005) — his earliest documented office — and "3.º supplente do delegado de policia de S. Paulo do Muriahé" by an act of 10 September 1902 (Minas Geraes gazette, 11 Sept 1902, GOV-0006, the official primary; reproduced in O Pharol, Juiz de Fora, 13 Sept 1902, NWS-0003). Recorded as occupations. Together they document his standing and Muriaé activity across 1899–1902 and add a civic role to his documented attorney/witness activity there (the FAN documents and the 1904 inventário). Distinct from the elder Barbacena Tenente-Coronel Simplício.
1 NOTE 1919 Toledo estate (Leopoldina): a partilha "folha de pagamento ao herdeiro" (PRB-0011) names Simplício José Ferreira Armond, "casado com Dona Eliza Balbina de Toledo", as heir and allots him a fazenda share (dwelling house, paiol, mill, halves of the engenho and ventilador, and mata-virgem and capoeira lands). He inherits in right of Eliza — a Toledo (in-law) estate — which corroborates his heir-by-marriage standing (previously cited only from PRB-0001/PRB-0002) and, if the retrieval agent's 1919 dating holds, extends his documented presence from "after 1902" (NWS-0003) toward c.1919. The folio names neither his own Armond parents nor the decedent whose estate is divided; the date and place are the agent's identification, off this page.
