1 NOTE Parents of Ladisláo Egídio Ferreira de Toledo (P-0056), confirmed by his 1787 baptism (PAR-0019) — extending Eliza's maternal Toledo line up to the Barbacena Ferreira de Toledo family. The couple is further corroborated by two daughters' marriages (PAR-0020 Anna Belizaria 1812; PAR-0021 Carolina Francelina 1816), which record the father in the "João José" variant; his preferred form is "Joaquim José Ferreira de Toledo", per his own 1786 marriage (PAR-0018), Ladisláo's 1787 baptism (PAR-0019) and the legible 1810 marriage (PAR-0023). His own parents were Gaspar Ferreira × Gertrudes Maria [de Toledo] (Vila Rica), now modelled as family F-0045 (P-0092 × P-0093); Ritta's were João Rodrigues [do Valle] × Izabel Ribeira (Borda do Campo), modelled as family F-0038 (P-0078 × P-0079). Both couples are named in Joaquim José and Ritta's own c.1786 marriage register (PAR-0018) — informant-reported parentage, held as strong-evidence; the F-0038 couple is additionally confirmed by Ritta's own 1764 baptism (PAR-0049).
1 NOTE The 1833 Barbacena inventory of Rita Angélica's estate (PRB-0010) directly names the couple's thirteen children — headed by "Ladisláo Egídio Ferreira" (child #1), directly confirming Ladisláo's parentage — and records that Rita died 9 February 1832, intestate, her widower Capitão Joaquim José being the inventariante. The other twelve children are recorded as documented_children above; the seven children of the deceased daughter Candida appear there as representantes (ages 3–13).
1 NOTE Officiant check (2026-08-12), testing the retrieval FINDINGS' claim that Ferreira Armond priests officiated the family's Barbacena sacraments 1780s–1821: NOT confirmed on our four held records. Legible officiants — PAR-0018 (1786 marriage): provision from Dr. José Batista das Flores, celebrant Pe. Antonio Teles, signed Vig. José Feliciano; PAR-0019 (1787 baptism): Vig. Dom Agostinho [Pinto] de Castro; PAR-0021 (1816 marriage): signed Vig. Manoel Sousa de Oliveira. The mid-entry celebrant names on PAR-0020 (1812) and PAR-0021 (1816) read "Rev. Pe. José Jorge/João Ferreira [surname worn]" — POSSIBLY the "José João Ferreira Armonde de Lima" the FINDINGS cite, but not legible on these ink-bled scans. Bounded negative; no Armond FAN entity created. A higher-resolution read of the PAR-0020/PAR-0021 celebrant lines would resolve it.
