1 TITL 1902 O Pharol (Juiz de Fora) official-acts notice naming Simplício José Ferreira Armond as 3rd substitute police delegate (supplente do delegado de polícia) of São Paulo do Muriaé
1 TEXT In its "Actos officiaes" column of 13 September 1902, the Juiz de Fora daily O Pharol reports that, by an act of 10 September 1902, the Minas Gerais police secretariat appointed the 1st, 2nd and 3rd substitutes to the police delegate of São Paulo do Muriaé: respectively Antonio Lourenço Dias, Marciano de Sousa Lopes, and Simplício José Ferreira Armond (P-0016) as the 3rd substitute (supplente). This documents Simplício's public/civic role at Muriaé in 1902 and places him living there — the same Simplício José Ferreira Armond who married Eliza Balbina de Toledo (P-0017) and is named in the 1881/1884 Toledo probate (PRB-0001, PRB-0002); it is NOT the elder Tenente-Coronel Simplício of Barbacena.
1 REPO @REPO0012@
