1 TITL Parish baptism of Maria, daughter of Amaro da Silva Xavier and Ignez Francisca de Lima, naming all four grandparents (23 August 1777, Minas do Piracatu / Manga parish)
1 TEXT Baptism on 23 August 1777 at the Minas do Piracatu (Manga parish, Bispado de Pernambuco) of Maria, born 12 August 1777, legitimate daughter of Amaro da Silva Xavier (P-0059) and Ignez Francisca de Lima (P-0060). The entry directly names all four grandparents: paternal — Amaro da Silva Barreto (P-0064), from Guimarães, Arcebispado de Braga (Portugal) × Perpétua da Silva (P-0065), from the Cidade de São Paulo; maternal — João Rodrigues de Mello (P-0066), from Viana, Arcebispado de Braga (Portugal) × Maria Francisca Cordeira (P-0067), from Villa de Ouro, Bispado de São Paulo. This is a primary source simultaneously establishing P-0059's and P-0060's parentage, extending both lines to Portugal (Braga archdiocese). Amaro da Silva Xavier (P-0059) is stated as native of the Freguesia de Nossa Senhora do Rio de Meia Ponte, Comarca do Goiás — conflicting with PAR-0023 (1810), which states both Amaro and Ignez as "naturais e batizados da Freguesia de Barbacena." The child in this entry is named "Maria" only; "Umbelina" does not appear in the visible text.
