1 NOTE Transcription: [Catholic parish marriage register, Grindel, Solothurn. Page 71. The section heading reads: "Catalogus. Eorum qui juxta normam S. Concilii Tridentini Sacro Matrimonii Vinculo juncti sunt. Incipiendo ab Anno Domini d.ni J. Chr. 1780" — i.e. a register of marriages contracted according to the norm of the (Roman Catholic) Council of Trent, begun in 1780. The Jacobus Werly × Elisabetha Borer entry is the fourth on the page:] Die 27ma Januarii 1782. In facie Ecclesiae fidem Matrimonialem Spoponderunt Honestus Juvenis Jacobus Werly et Elisabetha Borer ambo ex Grindel[-Erschwyl]. Testes fuerunt Heinricus Werly et Catharina Borer. [Translation: "On the 27th day of January 1782, in the face of the Church, the honourable youth Jacobus Werly [= Johann Jacob Wehrli] and Elisabetha Borer, both of Grindel[-Erschwyl], pledged the marital bond. The witnesses were Heinricus Werly [= Heinrich/Henri Wehrli] and Catharina Borer."] [Correction 2026-08-10: the earlier stored reading "ego … matrimonio junxi Jacobum Wehrliam …" was a paraphrase; the register's actual formula is "In facie Ecclesiae fidem Matrimonialem Spoponderunt …", verified against the image. Nearby entries name the parish priest (Parochus) Ursus Victor Grütz and use the same Tridentine formulae (denuntiationes/banns, in facie Ecclesiae, testes).]
