1 TITL Parish baptism of José (later José Cezário de Toledo Lima, P-0054), 10 March 1813, Matriz de Nossa Senhora do Pilar (São João del Rei) — names his parents Ladislau Egídio Ferreira and Dona Mathildes Maria de Jesus
1 TEXT The 1813 baptism register entry (Matriz de Nossa Senhora do Pilar, São João del Rei) of the child "José", baptised 10 March 1813, recorded as the legitimate son of Ladislau Egídio Ferreira (P-0056, register short form of Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo) and Dona Mathildes Maria de Jesus (P-0027). This is the baptism of José Cezário de Toledo Lima (P-0054): the child is entered under the single given name "José", and the identification rests on the exact double-parent match (both names in the distinctive register forms already attested for this couple), the parish (São João del Rei, where the parents had married on 8 May 1810, PAR-0023), and the 10 March 1813 date consistent with his inferred 1810s birth and adult-with-teenage children by 1867. His earliest vital record; it primary-confirms his parentage (family F-0027) and fixes his birth to on or shortly before 10 March 1813. Officiant Pe. Manoel Antônio de Castro; godparents a Tenente Coronel Caetano [José?] de Almeida and Dona Anna Francisca de Lima (both partly legible). A distinct entry lower on the same page baptises another "José" on 14 March 1813, son of the enslaved woman Silvana — not this person.
1 REPO @REPO0027@
