1 TITL 1877 Leopoldina notarial deed of sale by the Toledo grandchildren of their inherited Fazenda da Concórdia land, naming their grandmother Mathilde Maria de Jesus
1 TEXT A notarial deed of sale registered at Santo Antônio [dos Aribas?], Termo de Leopoldina, MG, on 25 May 1877, in which a set of Toledo-family grandchildren — Maria Bulandina de Jesus (wife of Manoel Marques Jorge), Josepha Olímpia, Maria [Perpétua/Porcelina] de Toledo, Matildes Olímpia da Paixão, Geraldo Augusto de Toledo and Ladisláo Egydio Ferreira de Toledo — sell to Capitão Antonio Belizandro dos Reis Meirelles two shares of cultivated land in the Fazenda da Concórdia that they inherited from their deceased grandmother (avó) Dona Mathildes Maria de Jesus. Same grandchild set and estate matriarch as the 1881 partilha (PRB-0001, which lists Eliza Balbina de Toledo among the "Primeiros Nettos") and the 1884 petition (PRB-0002).
