1 TITL 1867 Concórdia probate inventory of José Cesário de Toledo Lima and Claudina Brandina de Jesus — título de herdeiros listing nine children including Eliza Balbina de Toledo (P-0017) and a son named Simplício de Toledo (item 6, distinct from Simplício Armond P-0016)
1 TEXT The 1867 Concórdia (Districto do Rio Pardo, MG) probate inventory of José Cesário de Toledo Lima (P-0054) and his wife Claudina Brandina de Jesus (P-0055), both deceased by the opening date of 4 March 1867. The título de herdeiros lists their children (herdeiros); the page catalogued as p8 shows item 6 as "Simplicio José Ferreira de Tolledo, Solteiro de quatorze annos" — direct primary evidence that Simplício José Ferreira Armond (P-0016) is a son of José Cesário de Toledo Lima and Claudina Brandina de Jesus, settling his parentage. Items 7–9 (Ladisláo, Geraldo and an unnamed female infant) are also listed. The cover (gen1) explicitly names both deceased spouses: "José Cesario de Tolledo Lima / Claudina Brandina de Jesus." The certification is dated 7 March 1867, signed by J. de Bastos Pacheco (Escrivão dos Órfãos), before the judge Dr. Mortimário de Sousa Lintz; Aureliano de Sales Toledo (a sibling of JC) served as Curador of the minor heirs.
